packages/*/

# LIVE CREDENTIALS, never committed. This is not hypothetical and not about the developer's laptop:
# on a provisioned box the control plane writes `environment/.env` INSIDE this repository's checkout
# -- AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY and AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, refreshed via SSM. It is 0600
# root-owned and untracked, so it is invisible until someone runs `git add -A` in a deployed
# checkout, at which point live cloud credentials land in a PUBLIC repo. `hfdev env-publish` scans
# every published tree for live dotenv files precisely because this accident is known to happen.
#
# This repo is squarely in range: every calibration ladder runs on a provisioned SC box, i.e. on a
# deployed checkout with that file present. One line of deny costs nothing.
#
# No negation is needed here: no tracked file matches these patterns (checked, not assumed). If you
# ever add a legitimate `*.env`, negate that exact path -- do not weaken the rule.
.env
*.env

# NOTE: tasks/from_scratch_pca/tests/grader_pkg/ is a generated mirror of grader/reference/data
# (via scripts/build_task.py) but is intentionally COMMITTED, not ignored: the Harbor task tree
# must be self-contained at deploy time (no repo checkout of the source packages). CI runs
# `build_task.py --check` to fail the build if the committed mirror drifts from source.
